**Definition 8.1 (actual finite expansion recurrence).** For a schema $P$
at its complete actual entry $z$, let $\mathcal Q(P,z)$ return its
opcode/purpose vector, successor, ordinary-cell additions and finite-bit
additions. Its recursion is RCA Definition 11.5's literal expansion:

| Schema | Count and complete successor |
| --- | --- |
| One native row | Its unit opcode/purpose coordinate, actual PR57 local effect and one receipt |
| Sequence | First result, then second result at that complete successor; add vectors/additions |
| Test | The actual RD/CTL row, then its selected branch |
| Home/Tail | RD, exit at the actual boundary or move once and recurse |
| Append | EX; WR; MR, with net one ordinary cell |
| Base/Seek/unary copy | RCA's full counted scans on actual constructed unary words and entry heads |
| Assignment | Base; dry emission of all $r_2$ fields; actual emission, sep/F/seal; descriptor count/full descriptor; parity/purpose CTL |
| Word/list loop | Actual test, then zero on exit or actual finite body and recurrence at its successor |

Every new helper in §§2–6 has been reduced to this grammar. Find, sorting,
selection, graph enumeration, virtual Step, re-encoding and registry
assignment therefore have no independent unit-price oracle. Intermediate
register banks are real retained versions. Purpose changes and delimiters
are actual CTLs/appends, not annotations added without their rows.

For a continuing execution $\rho$ write $C(z)$ for the scalar sum through
$z$, $A_{\rm cell}(z)$ for all ordinary cell additions under RCA's boot
convention, and $b_{\rm ctl}(z)$ for actual constructed control bits.
Then, on that same execution,

$$
\operatorname{tick}(z)=C(z),\quad
\operatorname{fee}(z)=2C(z),\quad
\operatorname{storage}_{\rm native}(z)
 =S_0+b_{\rm ctl}(z)+8A_{\rm cell}(z)+8C(z).
\tag{PVC.9}
$$

Ordinary boot boundary cells are included in $A_{\rm cell}$, the irreducible
meter foundation in $S_0$, and all later receipts in $C$. Erasure,
retirement, registry replacement and inactive code remove no constructed
material from this accounting.

